  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire de La Clauvade, in Cuers, brings together 17 vets and 19 veterinary assistants according to its website. It is a general practice (preventive medicine, imaging, surgery, oncology, hospitalisation, on-site lab tests) that also runs its own emergency service: unlike UVDelta 83 or V2U Toulon, it is not an emergency-only clinic.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The clinic is open Monday to Saturday, 7:30am to 7:30pm (consultations by appointment, with emergency slots). Its website announces an emergency service 24/7, including weekends and public holidays: animals are seen without an appointment, but the clinic recommends phoning ahead on 04 94 48 55 54, the same number as for regular consultations.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call before you come, to describe your dog's symptoms and let the team get ready.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cuers and Pierrefeu-du-Var are easily reached from route de Nice.</p>
